{"repositoryId":802595107,"availability":"available","full":"SawyerHood/multisim","name":"multisim","description":"A demo of a multiplayer browser that imagines websites!","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":9,"forks":0,"created":"2024-05-18T18:27:25Z","updated":"2024-06-12T17:42:02Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://multisim.vercel.app","topics":["browser","genai","llm","multiplayer","nextjs","partykit","react","typescript","web"],"demo":"https://multisim.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-20T01:47:38.560Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-20T01:47:38.560Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-20T01:47:38.560Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T21:47:08.221Z","stars":9,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-20T01:47:38.560Z","stars":9,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This is a proof of concept to show what it could be like to have a fully multiplayer version of WebSim (a browser where an LLM generates the webpages).","This is demoware / a proof of concept. I wrote this over a weekend and decided that I don't want to flesh it out, but it is architecturally interesting so it is worth sharing.","There isn't any long term persistence of the pages or account management. Right now there is only a single hardcoded room as well. If you want to actually scale this you will need to be able to shard people into different servers. You really want the concept of a \"party\" or a \"universe\" where people can all jam on things together."],"features":["There is presence so you can see what pages other people are on.","If you are on the same page as someone else, you can see their multiplayer cursor","Multiple people can see a webpage stream in together","There is multiplayer chat so you can talk to other users"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SawyerHood/multisim/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ecdd9664db74d70311739fd1c689d276503b953366ae6ce33a5540f03b560007